1
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:11,090
Marilyn, you want coffee or tea?

2
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:25,900
Coffee, please.

3
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,800
I am so excited!

4
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,200
At this time tomorrow morning,

5
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:37,800
Grandpa will be sitting in the kitchen with us.

6
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,400
When does he arrive?

7
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:42,000
At six o'clock this evening.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,900
By plane?

9
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:47,800
No, by train.

10
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,700
Are we picking him up at the station?

11
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:50,900
Not Grandpa.

12
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:54,400
He doesn't want anybody picking him up.

13
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,500
He likes to be independent.

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:57,900
Huh.

15
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:01,300
Oh, let's go upstairs and prepare Grandpa's room.

16
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,000
Great! Let's do it!

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,400
Good morning, Mom.

18
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,200
Morning.

19
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,000
Well, hi, fellas.

20
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,200
Hello.

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,800
Hi, honey.

22
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:08,300
Morning, Marilyn.

23
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,900
We are going upstairs to set up Grandpa's room.

24
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:14,700
There's coffee ready.

25
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,600
I'm really excited about seeing Grandpa.

26
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:20,400
Me, too. Milk, please.

27
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,300
He's so funny.

28
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,900
He always makes me laugh.

29
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,000
I hope Grandpa's going to like living with us.

30
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,200
I think he will.

31
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,500
It just takes time to feel comfortable in a new place.

32
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,100
Won't he miss being in Florida?

33
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,200
Well, he will.

34
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,200
But I think he'll like being here with the family.

35
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,700
Are you sure about that?

36
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:39,200
It's crazy here most of the time.

37
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,700
But it's fun.

38
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,600
That's for sure.

39
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,800
You know,

40
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,400
maybe I'll put together some photos of Grandpa

41
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,100
as a "welcome" present.

42
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,200
That's a neat idea.

43
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,800
What can I do?

44
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:51,800
I've got it!

45
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:56,500
I have a picture of Grandpa and Dad and me in my wallet.

46
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,400
It's from the Fathers and Sons' Breakfast

47
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,900
at my junior high school graduation.

48
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:05,000
Oh, I remember this picture.

49
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,400
I'd really like to pick up Grandpa at the railroad station.

50
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,800
Railroad stations or airports.

51
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,600
Grandpa always tells us he'll get here by himself.

52
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:19,900
He's something!

53
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,500
Is this all Grandpa's stuff?

54
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,100
That's it.

55
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:28,500
But I'm sure he has a few bags with him on the train.

56
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:31,900
What's inside?

57
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:38,500
I don't know. It's locked.

58
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,300
Hi.

59
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:40,700
Oh, hi, darling.

60
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:41,700
Morning, Philip.

61
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,600
I want to put some of my good hangers in Grandpa's closet.

62
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:48,400
You know I'm very excited about his arrival.

63
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,900
We are, too.

64
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,100
Susan called early this morning.

65
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,000
She's unhappy

66
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,900
because she's had to go to Chicago on a business trip

67
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:57,600
and can't leave till tonight.

68
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,600
She wants to be here for Grandpa.

69
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,200
Well, Grandpa will be disappointed, too.

70
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,200
He loves Susan.

71
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:08,000
She always reminds him of Grandma.

72
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,600
Well, how's everything here?

73
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:17,650
Fine. We were just wondering about this trunk.

74
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:18,900
It's locked.

75
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,900
Oh. I have the key. Grandpa sent it to me.
